---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About RealmForge – The Algorithmic Fantasy Name Generator"
  description="Learn about RealmForge's phonetic syllable combinatorics, RPG naming algorithms, and worldbuilding tools."
  canonical="https://realmforge.app/about"
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-8">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-white/10">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold font-fantasy text-slate-100">
        About RealmForge
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-2">
        Empowering writers, game masters, and worldbuilders with authentic fantasy naming traditions.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-fantasy text-amber-200">
          The Philosophy Behind RealmForge
        </h2>
        <p>
          Naming is the first spark of fantasy immersion. When an adventurer steps into an inn called "The Drunken Dragon" or encounters a dwarven thane named "Thorin Stonebreaker", the entire history of the world comes into focus.
        </p>
        <p>
          Too many online name generators rely on simplistic dictionary lookups or produce unpronounceable gibberish. RealmForge was engineered by linguists and tabletop gamers to deliver phonetically authentic names based on real-world morphological roots, mythological traditions, and fantasy genre literature.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-fantasy text-amber-200">
          Algorithmic Syllable Combinatorics
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our generator engines execute two core models:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-100">Syllabic Root Synthesis:</strong> Deconstructs names into culture-specific prefixes, flowing middle linkers, and gendered suffix forms. For instance, elven names utilize soft fricatives and liquid consonants, while dwarven and orcish generators employ hard plosives and guttural stops.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-100">Compound Heraldry Combinatorics:</strong> Modeled after medieval Anglo-Norman taverns and heraldic house crests, pairing atmospheric adjectives, mythical beasts, and regional tavern specialties.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-fantasy text-amber-200">
          Zero Latency & Client-Side Privacy
        </h2>
        <p>
          Every name is computed instantly in your browser in under 5 milliseconds. We don't send your clicks or character ideas to remote servers, and your saved shortlist lives safely in your browser's LocalStorage. You can export your names to plain text anytime for your campaign binder.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
